IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bsma-types`
IMPORT `bsma-meetings`
IMPORT `bsma-developer`
IMPORT `bsma-corporation`
IMPORT `bsma-council`
IMPORT `bsma-boards-offences`

-- Building (Strata Management) Act 2004 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this strata development, is this matter validly decided by the
--    management corporation; may this person sit on its council; and what
--    does a proprietor in arrears now face?"
--
-- One answer through Goals 1, 3, 4 and 5. Goal 2 (the developer) and Goal 6
-- (offences, composition, service) answer their own questions in their
-- modules; each is listed in NOTES.md with the questions that invoke it.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Strata position` HAS
    `the resolution the matter needs`                IS A `Resolution kind`
    `the matter is validly decided`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Board may order on the matter`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the candidate is eligible for the council`      IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `interest runs on the contribution from`         IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the proprietor has committed the s 40(10) offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a charge may be lodged on the lot`              IS A BOOLEAN

@ref ss 2(2)-(7), 40, 43, 53, 101(6)
GIVEN s IS A `Strata case`
GIVETH A `Strata position`
`the strata position for` s MEANS
    `Strata position` WITH
        `the resolution the matter needs`                IS `the resolution needed for` (s's `matter`)
        `the matter is validly decided`                  IS `the matter is validly decided:` (s's `matter`) `, on` (s's `motion`)
        `a Board may order on the matter`                IS `a Board may order on a power exercised by` (`the resolution needed for` (s's `matter`))
        `the candidate is eligible for the council`      IS
            CONSIDER s's `candidate`
            WHEN JUST c  THEN JUST (`eligible for election to the council` c)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        `interest runs on the contribution from`         IS
            CONSIDER s's `contribution`
            WHEN JUST c  THEN `interest runs on the contribution from` c
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        `the proprietor has committed the s 40(10) offence` IS
            CONSIDER s's `contribution`
            WHEN JUST c  THEN `the proprietor commits the s 40(10) offence on` c `, as at` (s's `as at`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        `a charge may be lodged on the lot`              IS
            CONSIDER s's `contribution`
            WHEN JUST c  THEN `the corporation may lodge a charge for` c `, as at` (s's `as at`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
